          "locator": "Figure 3 and surrounding text",
          "role": "source"
        },
        "apparatus": {
          "name": "periodic_box_simulation",
          "description": "Periodic L x L homogeneous box with L=30, initial chemical potential mu_i=0.1, final chemical potential mu_f=20, coupling g=1, damping gamma=0.03, energy cutoff epsilon_cut=2.5 mu_f, and relaxation time t_r=10. Length, time, and temperature are measured in units of l=sqrt(hbar^2/(m E_sc)), hbar/E_sc, and E_sc/k_B respectively."
        },
        "background": "The system is a homogeneous Bose gas driven through the critical point by a linear quench of the chemical potential. The incompressible kinetic energy at the equilibration time is measured as a function of quench duration.",
