          "The incompressible kinetic energy at equilibration time varies with quench duration, and the variation depends on the temperature regime."
        ],
        "common_fixed_conditions": [
          {
            "condition_id": "simulation_parameters_common",
            "statement": "Periodic L x L homogeneous box with L=30, initial chemical potential mu_i=0.1, final chemical potential mu_f=20, coupling g=1, damping gamma=0.03, energy cutoff epsilon_cut=2.5 mu_f, and relaxation time t_r=10. Length, time, and temperature are measured in units of l=sqrt(hbar^2/(m E_sc)), hbar/E_sc, and E_sc/k_B respectively."
          },
          {
            "condition_id": "equilibration_time_definition",
            "statement": "The equilibration time t_eq is determined by analyzing N_C/L^2, locating the global maximum of its second derivative, then identifying the subsequent interval (t1,t2) where the second derivative is <= -Delta with Delta=10% of that maximum, and setting t_eq=t2."
          }
        ],
        "controls": [
          {
            "name": "tau_Q",
            "description": "Quench duration of the linear chemical-potential ramp mu(t) = mu_i + (mu_f - mu_i) t / tau_Q, driving the system through the critical point.",
            "unit": "dimensionless (scaled units)",
            "minimum": 100.0,
            "maximum": 1000.0,
            "allowed_values": []
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "name": "E_i",
            "description": "Total incompressible kinetic energy at equilibration time, defined as E_i = (1/2) integral |u_i(r, t_eq)|^2 d^2r = integral_0^infinity E_i(k) dk, where u_i is the incompressible (solenoidal) component of the density-weighted velocity field u = |Psi_C| v.",
            "unit": "dimensionless (scaled units)",
            "statistic": "Deterministic central value of the source-reported quantitative relation.",
            "uncertainty": "Any source-reported uncertainty is retained as provenance and is not sampled or propagated into this query.",
